Z||000018||poupas||06-11-2001||05:23 AM||||I have a question for everyone that voted to have the Fiero back in production, why? Think about why you like Fieros:<BR>     they are sporty<BR>     they have two seats<BR>     they have mid-engine<BR>     they were only made for 5 years<BR>     Why do you like a Fiero? Would you actually like Fieros as much is they have been in production since '84. That would be 17 generations of Fieros. Everyone would have one.<BR>   This is a question to everyone that voted to bring the Fiero back, How good would your Fiero look compared to a 2002 Fiero, or a 2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008 etc.. All our cars would look like relics. If they made them that nice in the '20th century, imagine the 21st. <BR>  Do you like, lets say, how the 1987 Toyota Celica looks, or the 2001? Or does it matter? Since they have been making the same car for 20 odd years.<BR>  We all own cars that have only been developed for 5 years, be proud to own one. And that no one else will ever buy a brand new Fiero again.||||reg||1
